    "explanation": "BH₃ adds B to the less hindered carbon (C2) and H to C1, syn. Oxidation replaces B with OH with retention, so the OH is trans to the methyl. Both enantiomers form: racemic trans-2-methylcyclohexanol.",
    "tip": "OH goes where the H was; syn addition puts it trans to the methyl."
